❮ Java Keywords

Thevarkeyword allows a variable to be initialized without having to declare its type. The type of the variable depends on the type of the data that is being assigned to it.

Thevarkeyword was introduced in Java 10.

Read more about variables in ourJava Variables Tutorial.

❮ Java Keywords

### Code Snippets

```
Example
Use
var
to declare variables:
public class Main {
  public int test = 10;

  public static void main(String[] args) {
    var x = 5;
    var main = new Main();
    System.out.println(x);
    System.out.println(main.test);
  }
}
Try it Yourself »
```
